{"uid":"lazyc2/security/command_allowlist.py","name":"command_allowlist.py","qualname":"lazyc2/security/command_allowlist.py","kind":"module","file":"lazyc2/security/command_allowlist.py","line":1,"end_line":141,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Command allowlist policy for the LazyOwn C2 ``/api/run`` endpoint.","description":"Contract: this module gates arbitrary command execution so only commands\nwhose first whitespace-delimited token is on a configurable allowlist can\nreach the LazyOwn shell. Shell metacharacters are always rejected as a\ndefence-in-depth check independent of the allowlist.\n\nInvariants:\n\n1. The first non-whitespace token of the command is matched against the\n   allowlist in a case-insensitive way.\n2. Any of the characters ``;``, ``|``, ``&``, ``$``, ``>``, ``<``,\n   backtick, newline, carriage return, or backslash causes a rejection\n   with reason :class:`CommandRejectionReason.SHELL_METACHAR`.\n3. Empty / whitespace / non-string commands reject with reason\n   :class:`CommandRejectionReason.EMPTY`.\n4. When ``audit_log_path`` is set, every decision is appended as a single\n   JSON line so the operator can review what was attempted.\n\nConfig keys owned:\n\n- ``c2_api_command_allowlist`` (CSV string, default\n  ``\"ping,set,show,help,status,sessions,sitrep,gets,get,downloader,getosession,osession,setar,getar,session,clean\"``)","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["lazyc2/security/command_allowlist.py::CommandRejectionReason","lazyc2/security/command_allowlist.py::CommandDecision","lazyc2/security/command_allowlist.py::CommandAllowlist"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
